        "text_RYVXj3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Sleeping in clean air supports better rest and reduced allergy symptoms. A quiet purifier runs whisper-quiet at night while removing dust, pollen, and pet dander.<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/blog-bedrooms\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Bedroom air purifiers</span></a> should operate at low noise levels to avoid disturbing sleep while maintaining effective filtration.</p><p>The Blue Pure 211i Max cleans 674 square feet in just 12.5 minutes with a 410 CFM CADR rating, making it ideal for larger bedrooms or primary suites where consistent overnight purification matters most.</p><h4><strong>Living Rooms</strong></h4>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_rrTkpH": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
